UID:0f78405acd722973453b0857033308d0@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Sale\n      \n\n\n\n\n\nSebTown Clay Club: Wednesday Afterscho
 ol Clay Club (Ages 6-9)\n\n  \n    \n      \n      from $65.00\n    \n  \n
 \nSebTown Clay Club meets on Wednesdays from 1:30-4:30pm.Students May Arri
 ve Late. Join us on Wednesday’s for a special Youth Clay Club\,  focused
  on fostering space for ceramics creative freedoms while exploring clay bu
 ilding techniques to make themed creations each week. Every three weeks\, 
 we have a new theme that allows students to explore their imaginations and
  create what they want to see. In Sebastopol\, students are out of school 
 early on Wednesdays\, as early as 1:00pm. Instead of focusing on a project
  driven\, or specific skill\, we are offering a ceramics series in which s
 tudents are encouraged to create what they would like with the supervision
  and guidance of an instructor to facilitate the learning needs of the stu
 dent. Students will be given an outside play break from 2:45-3:15 where th
 ey can enjoy snacks and group games. This can be purchased as a 9 session 
 bundle\, 3-session series\, or drop-in (single day) registrations.3-Sessio
 n Series: $105 + $25 Clay Fee9 Sessions: $315 + $75 Clay Fee (Currently on
  sale for early bird registrations $30 off!) Drop-In Same-Day Sessions: $4
 0 + $25 Clay Fee SebTown Clay Club SessionsCreepy Cryptids\, Monsters\, an
 d Ghouls: October 7th\, October 14th\, October 21stUnder the Fantasea: Goi
 ng Underwater : October 28th\, November 4th\, November 18thCerama-Mini Man
 ia: Faeries\, Goblins\, and Elves - Oh My! December 2nd\, December 9th\, D
 ecember 16thPlease note that SebTown Clay Club Under the Fantasea skips No
 vember 11th in observation of Veterans Day. About the Instructor: Rogelio 
 Cruz is our Youth Arts Coordinator who will be facilitating and teaching t
 his program. Rogelio Cruz is a visual and performing artist born and raise
 d in Sonoma County. They graduated from San Francisco State University wit
 h a BA in Fine Arts and a minor in dance. Rogelio is driven by a dedicatio
 n to furthering the accessibility of art and arts\, and their teaching phi
 losophy is centered around facilitating a space for all to freely learn an
 d grow in their creative process. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                  Sessi
 ons:\n                \n\n\n\n                      Select Sessions\n     
                \nCreepy Cryptids\, Monsters\, and Ghouls: October 7th\, Oc
 tober 14th\, October 21st\nUnder the Fantasea: Going Underwater : October 
