BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Introduction to Asemic Writing — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\
 , California
DTSTART:20261212T000000
DTEND:20261213T000000
UID:00c6d7e8985a23a860f9fa261b5b1491@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Introduction to Asemic Writing (December 12th)\n\n  \n    \n  
     \n        \n          $175.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nIntroduct
 ion to Asemic Writing Saturday\, December 12th\, 2026 - 10:00am-4:00pm$160
 .00 + $15.00 Materials Fee = $175.00 RegistrationClass Limited to 12 Stude
 ntsRegister now for both of Sherrie Lovler’s Workshops this weekend\, an
 d receive $20.00 off your total order! Use code SHRRLVLR-EARLYBIRD-1212132
 6 to claim your discount!December 12th: Introduction to Asemic WritingDece
 mber 13th: Wabi-Sabi Ink Painting: Finding Beauty in ImperfectionClass Des
 cription: Asemic writing is the creation of marks that resemble handwritin
 g but carry no literal meaning or readable text. It is the word before wor
 ds form—the voice too distant to be understood—a universal expression 
 without country or dialect.We’ll begin with a slideshow exploring the ri
 ch history and possibilities of asemic writing\, from ancient scripts and 
 symbols to the calligraphic line and the work of contemporary artists. Fro
 m there\, you’ll begin your own exploration using ink\, watercolor\, and
  a variety of tools on paper.Through guided exercises and playful experime
 ntation\, we’ll explore line\, gesture\, rhythm\, repetition\, and space
 . You’ll discover how asemic marks can infiltrate and transform your exi
 sting artwork or become works of art in their own right.You’ll leave wit
 h a collection of new work\, fresh approaches to mark-making\, and a deepe
 r trust in your own intuition and expressive voice. My intention is to gui
 de you beyond casual scribbling toward authentic marks—marks that arise 
 from the heart and become uniquely your own.All levels welcome.IMPORTANT: 
 CLICK HERE FOR THE LIST OF REQUIRED MATERIALS FOR THIS CLASS. Not all mate
 rials are provided\, please see the list of request materials above. If yo
 u have any questions regarding materials\, please contact your instructor:
  sherrie@artandpoetry.com—About the Instructor: Sherrie Lovler is a pain
 ter\, poet\, and teacher whose work bridges Western calligraphy and the ex
 pressive spirit of Asian brush painting. With a BA in Studio Art\, she has
  taught for several decades at international calligraphy conferences and i
 nstitutions including Ghost Ranch\, Northern Arizona University\, and loca
 l art centers. Her paintings explore the space between writing and image. 
 Inspired by Asian brushwork and the Japanese aesthetic of wabi-sabi\, she 
 embraces imperfection\, spontaneity\, and fluid mark-making. Sumi ink\, ge
 sture\, color\, and asemic writing become an abstract visual language. She
  is the author\, illustrator\, and designer of the award-winning book On S
 ofter Ground. Her latest book\, Distant Voices\, explores art as a collabo
 ration with nature\, poetry\, and unseen influences. She participates in S
 onoma County Art Trails\, Art at the Source\, and presented a solo exhibit
 ion at Gallery Route One in Point Reyes Station in 2025. www.artandpoetry.
 com\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n     
      \n            \n              \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/introduction-to-asemic-writin
 g
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
