DESCRIPTION:Explore Gel Plate Printing - December 12th\n\n  \n    \n      
 \n        \n          $130.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nAll images sh
 own are property of the instructor\, Catherine CruzSaturday\, December 12t
 h\, 2026\; 11 AM – 3 PMFee: $115 + $15 materials feeAge: 16+ Class Descr
 iption: Explore the art of gel plate printing with French-American artist 
 Catherine Cruz. You will learn to create beautiful monoprint designs on pa
 per using a gel plate and acrylic paint. You will take home lots of prints
  that can be used for creating collage\, mixed media art or greeting cards
 . This class is perfect for anyone wanting to learn this unique monoprint 
 style and is perfect for beginners.The instructor will teach you the basic
  skills for using this fun tool\, from printing textural backgrounds\, to 
 layering colors and using a variety of unexpected tools.Note: Image transf
 er technique is not part of this class.What you will learn: Methods for ap
 plying paint and pulling successful printsTechniques for creating intricat
 e layered designsCreative use of mark-making tools and masksStrategies for
  combining techniquesThe instructor will provide a gel plate\, brayer\, ac
 rylic paint and mark-making tools. A variety of papers will be provided bu
 t we encourage you to bring your own papers to experiment with.Click below
  for Materials ListIMPORTANT: Instructions for where to purchase your mate
 rials and how to prepare them is provided in the attached PDF. The instruc
 tor will start the class with a demonstration so please arrive a few minut
 es early to get set up so we can start on time.  We will take a short brea
 k for lunch between 12:30 and 1:00 pm so bring your lunch and a beverage. 
   This class is held in the Little Red Hen Dining Room at the Sebastopol C
 enter for the Arts at 282 South High Street\, Sebastopol\, CA 95472.About 
 the instructor: Catherine Cruz is a French-American artist whose work is i
 nformed by textures and patterns created by the passing of time and the ef
 fects of the natural elements on the built environment.  She holds a Bache
 lor of Science in interior design and she worked in the field of architect
 ural design and green building certification for over 25 years.  She has t
 aught collage and mixed media workshops in the Bay Area and in France sinc
 e 2019\, and this is her fifth year at the Sebastopol Center for the Arts.
   Her studio is located in Sebastopol and she participates in Art Trails O
 pen Studios.  You may contact Catherine at beyouartstudio@gmail.com.  Chec
 k out Catherine’s other classes here:  https://wwws.sebarts.org/visual-a
 rts-classes.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n          \n            \n              \n                Add to cart
