BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wabi-Sabi Ink Painting: Finding Beauty in Imperfection — Sebasto
 pol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20261213T000000
DTEND:20261214T000000
UID:e97f277833768664401a5e604c9b26d6@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Wabi-Sabi Ink Painting: Finding Beauty in Imperfection (Decemb
 er 13th)\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $175.00\n        \n     
  \n    \n  \n\nWabi-Sabi Ink Painting: Finding Beauty in Imperfection (Dec
 ember 13th) Sunday\, December 13th\, 2026 - 10:00am-4:00pm$160.00 + $15.00
  Materials Fee = $175.00 RegistrationClass Limited to 12 StudentsRegister 
 now for both of Sherrie Lovler’s Workshops this weekend\, and receive $2
 0.00 off your total order! Use code SHRRLVLR-EARLYBIRD-12121326 to claim y
 our discount!December 12th: Introduction to Asemic WritingDecember 13th: W
 abi-Sabi Ink Painting: Finding Beauty in ImperfectionClass Description: St
 ep into a creative space where intuition leads and imperfection becomes be
 auty. This immersive workshop explores abstract painting through both East
 ern and Western perspectives\, blending meditation\, movement\, and mark-m
 aking to create expressive\, finished paintings.Rooted in the Japanese aes
 thetic of wabi-sabi\, we’ll release the desire for perfection and welcom
 e the unexpected. Discover the quiet magic that happens when ink meets wat
 er\, gestures emerge without planning\, and the body and breath guide the 
 brush.We’ll begin with gentle centering and meditation\, preparing you t
 o work from the heart and engage your whole body in the creative process. 
 You’ll practice painting the ensō—the Zen circle expressing wholeness
 \, presence\, movement\, and stillness. Using Asian brushes\, ink\, and wa
 tercolor on paper\, you will create calligraphic paintings with layered ac
 cents that bring depth\, atmosphere\, and emotion to your work.Through gui
 ded exercises and open-ended exploration\, you’ll learn to trust your in
 tuition\, loosen up\, and respond to what unfolds. You’ll leave with a c
 ollection of expressive paintings and new ways to bring spontaneity and fr
 eedom into your artwork.All levels welcome.IMPORTANT: CLICK HERE FOR THE L
 IST OF REQUIRED MATERIALS FOR THIS CLASS. Not all materials are provided\,
  please see the list of request materials above. If you have any questions
  regarding materials\, please contact your instructor: sherrie@artandpoetr
 y.com—About the Instructor: Sherrie Lovler is a painter\, poet\, and tea
 cher whose work bridges Western calligraphy and the expressive spirit of A
 sian brush painting. With a BA in Studio Art\, she has taught for several 
 decades at international calligraphy conferences and institutions includin
 g Ghost Ranch\, Northern Arizona University\, and local art centers. Her p
 aintings explore the space between writing and image. Inspired by Asian br
 ushwork and the Japanese aesthetic of wabi-sabi\, she embraces imperfectio
 n\, spontaneity\, and fluid mark-making. Sumi ink\, gesture\, color\, and 
 asemic writing become an abstract visual language. She is the author\, ill
 ustrator\, and designer of the award-winning book On Softer Ground. Her la
 test book\, Distant Voices\, explores art as a collaboration with nature\,
  poetry\, and unseen influences. She participates in Sonoma County Art Tra
 ils\, Art at the Source\, and presented a solo exhibition at Gallery Route
  One in Point Reyes Station in 2025. www.artandpoetry.com\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \
 n              \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/wabi-sabi-ink-painting-findin
 g-beauty-in-imperfection-1
